    "body": "## Problem\n\nMulti-line clipboard content set via OSC 52 from a `:terminal` collapses to a single line for command providers (tmux, xclip, wl-copy, …): `term_clipboard_set()` passes the decoded payload as a single multi-line list element, and writing such a list to a job's stdin encodes each embedded newline as NUL (`:help channel-lines`). The payload is also truncated at the first NUL byte.\n\n## Solution\n\nPass the payload to the clipboard provider as a Blob (as suggested in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40271#discussion_r3441747807), without changing the contract for existing providers:\n\n- `save_tv_as_string()` handles `VAR_BLOB`, so `system()`, `systemlist()` and `chansend()` write Blob input to stdin verbatim (replaces chansend's bespoke Blob branch).\n- Command providers and the provider cache receive the Blob unchanged.\n- Function copy providers receive a List of lines by default (existing `g:clipboard` configs are unaffected); the new `g:clipboard` `\"blob\"` key opts into receiving the Blob. The builtin OSC 52 provider opts in, so terminal-to-host OSC 52 forwarding is byte-exact.\n- `get_clipboard()` splits a Blob paste payload into register lines (NUL stored as NL, `:help NL-used-for-Nul`) and rejects a NULL Blob. Oversized (> 2 GiB) OSC 52 payloads are dropped: Blob length is `int`.\n\nDocs: `provider.txt`, `news.txt`, `system()`.\n\nTests: function-provider default and `\"blob\"` opt-in; NUL and trailing-newline handling; command provider gets raw bytes on stdin (with and without `cache_enabled`); builtin OSC 52 forwarding; Blob paste splitting; NULL-Blob rejection; `system()`/`systemlist()` Blob input.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "closed_at": null,
